.TH POWERGOV.CONF 5 "July 2026" "powergov 1.13.0" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
powergov.conf \- persistent configuration for the powergov daemon
.SH DESCRIPTION
The file
.I /etc/powergov.conf
stores settings loaded at daemon start and updated when runtime changes are
applied through
.BR powergov (1),
.BR powergov-ui (1),
or the control socket. Lines beginning with
.B #
are comments. Keys use
.BR KEY=value
syntax (no spaces around
.BR = ).
.PP
Template in the source tree:
.IR config/powergov.conf .
.SH USER MODE
.TP
.B USER_MODE
One of:
.BR max-battery
(default),
.BR balanced ,
.BR performance ,
or
.BR custom .
Controls overall aggressiveness on battery. See
.IR Documentation/configuracion.md .
.SH FEATURES
.TP
.B FEATURES
Comma-separated list of enabled subsystems. Valid names:
.RB governor ,
.BR epp ,
.BR freq_cap ,
.BR turbo ,
.BR platform ,
.BR runtime_pm ,
.BR peripheral_pm ,
.BR disk_pm ,
.BR pcie_aspm ,
.BR bluetooth_pm .
.SH BATTERY SAFE
.TP
.B BATTERY_SAFE_THRESHOLD
Integer 0\(en100. 0 disables battery-safe mode. Values 1\(en100 block the
performance governor when state of charge is at or below the threshold.
.SH LOGGING
.TP
.B LOG_LEVEL
0 (off) through 4 (debug). Default 3 (info).
.TP
.B DEV_LOG
0 or 1. When 1, structured developer log is written to
.IR /var/log/powergov/powergov.log .
.SH STATE MACHINE THRESHOLDS
Fractions of CPU load (0.0\(en1.0) for the internal governor state machine:
.TP
.B THRESHOLD_LOW
Default 0.25 \(en POWERSAVE versus BALANCED boundary.
.TP
.B THRESHOLD_MID
Default 0.60 \(en exit from PERFORMANCE.
.TP
.B THRESHOLD_HIGH
Default 0.75 \(en enter PERFORMANCE.
.SH CPU AND BATTERY LEVELS
.TP
.B FREQ_CAP_BATTERY
Percent of hardware max frequency (50\(en100, default 80) applied on battery.
.TP
.B LOW_BATTERY
SOC percent (5\(en50, default 15) for survival profile (stricter freq cap).
.SH PERIPHERALS (CUSTOM MODE)
Used when
.B USER_MODE=custom
and feature
.B peripheral_pm
is enabled:
.TP
.B PERIPHERAL_WIFI
.TP
.B PERIPHERAL_SATA
.TP
.B PERIPHERAL_AUDIO
Each 0 or 1 (default 1). WiFi uses
.BR iw (8);
audio uses HDA codec power_save.
.SH CUSTOM MODE FLAGS
.TP
.B CUSTOM_ALLOW_PERFORMANCE
0 or 1. Allow performance governor on battery in custom mode.
.TP
.B CUSTOM_RUNTIME_AGGRESSIVE
0 or 1. Aggressive PCI/USB runtime PM in custom mode.
.SH CONTEXT REACTIVE BOOST (v1.13+)
.TP
.B LID_AGGRESSIVE
0 or 1 (default 1). Boost when lid is closed.
.TP
.B DISPLAY_AGGRESSIVE
0 or 1 (default 1). Boost when logind
.B IdleHint
is true (screen off / session idle).
.TP
.B CONTEXT_REQUIRE_LOW_LOAD
0 or 1 (default 1). Require low CPU load before context boost.
.TP
.B CONTEXT_LOW_LOAD_PCT
Integer percent (default 15). Maximum CPU load for context boost when
.B CONTEXT_REQUIRE_LOW_LOAD
is 1.
.PP
See
.IR Documentation/contexto-reactivo.md .
.SH MEMORY-AWARE POLICY (v1.14+)
Avoid aggressive saving when the kernel reports memory pressure:
.TP
.B MEMORY_AWARE
0 or 1 (default 1). Enable PSI/swap-aware policy floor.
.TP
.B MEMORY_PSI_SOME_PCT
.TP
.B MEMORY_PSI_FULL_PCT
.TP
.B MEMORY_SWAP_PAGES_TICK
.TP
.B MEMORY_SWAP_PAGES_SEVERE
Thresholds for stressed/severe classification (see
.IR Documentation/memory-aware.md ).
.SH RUNTIME TUNING
Thresholds, peripherals, custom flags, and context keys can also be changed at
runtime via the control socket commands
.B SET_TUNING
and
.B QUERY_TUNING
without editing this file manually; the daemon persists accepted values here.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/powergov.conf
This configuration file.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR powergov (1),
.BR powergov (8),
.BR powergov-ui (1),
.IR Documentation/configuracion.md .
.SH AUTHOR
Iván Ezequiel Rodriguez.
